License decision deferred to Week 5.

Reason: I don't care much about the license at this stage, and I want
other people to be able to take the project. My leading candidate is MIT,
with GPL-3.0-only as the backup. The question that will settle it: do I
want others free to take this and close-source their own changes (MIT
allows it), or do I require that improvements stay open (GPL requires it)?

Candidate license texts read at their primary source on 2026-09-20:
https://spdx.org/licenses/MIT.html
https://spdx.org/licenses/GPL-3.0-only.html

